            'adv.cea.deltaNote': 'Δ % = 100 × (HRMA − CEA) / CEA. No pass/fail threshold is applied: none is sourced for the difference between two equilibrium codes. Advisory only — this comparison changes none of the numbers HRMA publishes.',
            'adv.cea.deliveredIdeal': 'Delivered c* of this run: no c* efficiency was applied (no measured value for this propellant pair), so the design uses the ideal c* in the table. A real motor delivers less.',
            'adv.cea.deliveredLine': 'Delivered c* used by this run\'s design (a separate quantity, not compared above): {cd} m/s = η_c* {eta} × theoretical {ci} m/s.',
            'adv.cea.verificationNote': 'What this comparison is: code VERIFICATION — two ideal equilibrium codes give the same answer under the same assumptions (complete combustion, adiabatic chamber, infinite-area combustor). It is not VALIDATION, which needs measured motor data (AIAA G-077; NASA-STD-7009A). Delivered performance is lower than the CEA ideal.',
            'adv.cea.derivedNote': '† Derived from the same code\'s own published values with one identity used in both directions: C_F,vac = C_F + ε·p_e/p_c and Isp = C_F·c*/g0 (Sutton & Biblarz, 9th ed., Eq. 3-30).',
            'adv.cea.exitOmitted': 'Exit-plane rows are not compared: HRMA\'s exit station for this run is not a shifting-equilibrium solution at ε.',
            'adv.cea.hrmaAboveCeiling': 'HRMA\'s chamber temperature ({tc} K) is above that limit (NASA polynomials extrapolated).',
            'adv.cea.hrmaSource': 'HRMA column: Cantera {version} chemical equilibrium with mechanism {mechanism} ({description}); its thermo data are valid up to {ceiling} K.',
            'adv.cea.pointLine': 'Same operating point as this run — Pc = {pc} bar, O/F = {of}, ε = {eps} — and the same propellant definition; equilibrium (shifting) expansion, infinite-area combustor.',
